       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, which is about double the maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin (2,550 mg). Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPlease don't enter a corrected dose on your own, and please check the order with the prescribing physician before anything is entered. If the physician confirms a different dose, a licensed clinician should enter it, or I can enter it once they give me the exact drug, dose, route, frequency, and any note they want included. The prescriber should also confirm whether this was meant to be extended-release, which has a lower maximum of 2,000 mg per day."
