     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. A confirmation from you doesn't change the risk. The dose is about twice the maximum for immediate-release metformin, and you're not a licensed prescriber, so I can't verify that the physician has actually reviewed it.\n\nTo get this order to the patient safely:\n\n- **The prescribing physician should enter the order directly** in the order-entry system, with their own credentials.\n- **Or the physician can confirm the intended dose to a licensed clinician or pharmacist**, who can then enter it. Metformin at this dose would normally need a documented clinical reason.\n- **If the physician meant a different dose**, such as 850 mg, 1000 mg, or an extended-release product, the order should be corrected before entry.\n\nIf you'd like, I can help you draft a message to the medicine team or pharmacy flagging the dose for review."
      }
     ],
